+[![Historical Go memory and pending identity integration](docs/diagrams/memory-identity-en.svg)](docs/diagrams/memory-identity-en.svg)
+
+**Memory carries context, never authority.** An experience or procedure from
+verified lessons learned can be admitted, versioned and explicitly selected for
+a future task. Received context retains its conditions and provenance. Withdrawal
+affects future selections; it does not erase context already delivered. This
+flow describes the historical Go foundation; Rust qualification and shared
+memory usage rights remain open.
+
+**Identity distinguishes the initiator, logical agent and execution instance.**
+The internal kernel checks the plan, grants, delegation, expiry and revocation.
+These components do not establish protection of every launcher, authenticated
+human identity or provider confinement. Integration with public operations and
+memory usage remains unfinished.
+
+For example, selecting a verification procedure for a new mission does not give
+an agent permission to create a worker or approve a business action.
+
